# P18-V01 Remoting custom-header alias and factory behavior — 2026-10-17T12:48:21Z

- Repository branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`.
- Java oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1 commit
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`; the oracle checkout remained
  read-only.
- Added `SharedCommandHeader<T>` so a caller-retained clone and the command's
  custom header share mutations. Added fallible response/error header factories
  for Java reflection behavior: response construction returns no command when
  header construction fails, and error-response construction reports
  `NullPointerException` after consuming the opaque ID.
- Extended the invoked Java runtime fixture for both mutation directions,
  missing/inaccessible/throwing default constructors, and request-ID delta.
  Fixture SHA-256: `ed7f13b1ba8b0d91ef6dd63683ff3630c9b8b9212ae2770484bdfc29f15469be`.
